  "notes": "CONJUGATION: Godan く-verb. {見|み}え{透|す}く → {見|み}え{透|す}いて → {見|み}え{透|す}いた.\n\nUSAGE:\nAlmost always used in the past participle form {見|み}え{透|す}いた as a modifier: {見|み}え{透|す}いた{嘘|うそ} (an obvious lie), {見|み}え{透|す}いた{手|て} (a transparent ploy). Rarely used in other conjugated forms.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {見|み}え{透|す}いた{嘘|うそ} (a transparent lie)\n- {見|み}え{透|す}いた{手口|てぐち} (an obvious trick)\n- {見|み}え{透|す}いたお{世辞|せじ} (obvious flattery)",
